        "original_id": "08883002-7256-5063-a392-5d3cfd4b70cd",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Muztagh Ata, Manaslu, Chakragil, Kashgar, Kongur Tagh, Tibetan Plateau\n- Topics: mountain heights, mountain locations\n\nFacts:\n- Muztagh Ata, or Muztagata, is 7,509 metres high and is the second-highest mountain forming the northern edge of the Tibetan Plateau.\n- Manaslu, also known as Kutang, is the eighth-highest mountain in the world at 8,163 metres above sea level.\n- Chakragil is located about 100 km southwest of Kashgar, about 60 km due north of Muztagh Ata, and 37 km northwest of Kongur Tagh.",
